       x1BzDq6nKDfXvGXicpxO8Zc46aQyw6aQcn0Llh0cvpYRy9HUuGSXGDcOpHiO4dByR1Dc5lx1
       Fg9HU5IuYsuXLmnTlnEddHMXLP/Z
      </office:binary-data>
     </draw:image>
    </draw:frame></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P58" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1588_447025415"/>Perché serve una funzione di attivazione?<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1588_447025415"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Senza una funzione non lineare, anche una rete composta da molti strati si comporterebbe essenzialmente come un’unica trasformazione lineare. Le funzioni di attivazione permettono alla rete di rappresentare relazioni più complesse.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Nei modelli moderni vengono usate funzioni come ReLU, GELU o varianti simili. Per esempio:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Object23" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:y="-0.406cm" svg:width="3.514cm" svg:height="0.522cm" draw:z-index="28"><draw:object>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
       <semantics>
        <mrow>
         <mtext>ReLU</mtext>
         <mrow>
          <mrow>
           <mo fence="true" form="prefix" stretchy="true">(</mo>
           <mrow>
            <mi>z</mi>
           </mrow>
           <mo fence="true" form="postfix" stretchy="true">)</mo>
          </mrow>
          <mo stretchy="false">=</mo>
          <mi mathvariant="italic">max</mi>
         </mrow>
         <mrow>
          <mo fence="true" form="prefix" stretchy="true">(</mo>
          <mrow>
           <mrow>
            <mn>0</mn>
            <mi>,</mi>
            <mi>z</mi>
           </mrow>
          </mrow>
          <mo fence="true" form="postfix" stretchy="true">)</mo>
         </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0">&quot;ReLU&quot; left( z right) = max left( 0, z right)</annotation>
       </semantics>
      </math>
     </draw:object><draw:image>
      <office:binary-data>VkNMTVRGAQAxAAAAAAAAAAEAGwAAAAkAAAAAAAAAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAcgHAAAo
       AQAAVQAAAJYAAQACAAAACQCLAAEAAgAAAP//gQABABAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMcHAAAnAQAAiwAB
       AAIAAAAAGJUAAQAEAAAAAAAAAJYAAQACAAAACQCLAAEAAgAAAB8AigABAEgAAAAFAEIAAAAQ
       AExpYmVyYXRpb24gU2VyaWYAAAAAAADwAAAAAAAAAAAABQAAAAAAAAD/AwAAAAAAAAABAP8D
       AAAAAAAAAAAAAACIAAEAAgAAAAEAhwABAAUAAAD/////AIYAAQAEAAAAAAAAAHIAAgAgAAAA
       BgAAAOYAAAAEAFJlTFVLAgAAAAAEAAQAUgBlAEwAVQCMAAEAAAAAAIsAAQACAAAAHwCKAAEA
       QgAAAAUAPAAAAAoAT3BlblN5bWJvbAAAdwAAAPUAAAD//wAAAAAFAAAAAAAAAP8DAAAAAAAA
       AAEA/wMAAAAAAHcAAAAAAIgAAQACAAAAAQCHAAEABQAAAP////8AhgABAAQAAAAAAAAAcgAC
       ABoAAAB0AgAA4QAAAAEAAAAoACgAAAAAAAEAAQAoAIwAAQAAAAAAiwABAAIAAAAfAIoAAQBI
       AAAABQBCAAAAEABMaWJlcmF0aW9uIFNlcmlmAAAAAAAA8AAAAAAAAAAAAAUAAAAAAAIA/wMA
       AAAAAAAAAQD/AwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAiAABAAIAAAABAIcAAQAFAAAA/////wCGAAEABAAAAAAA
       AAByAAIAFwAAAL4CAADmAAAAAQB6XQAAAAAAAQABAHoAjAABAAAAAACLAAEAAgAAAB8AigAB
       AEIAAAAFADwAAAAKAE9wZW5TeW1ib2wAAHcAAAD1AAAA//8AAAAABQAAAAAAAAD/AwAAAAAA
       AAABAP8DAAAAAAB3AAAAAACIAAEAAgAAAAEAhwABAAUAAAD/////AIYAAQAEAAAAAAAAAHIA
       AgAaAAAANwMAAOEAAAABAAAAKQAoAAAAAAABAAEAKQCMAAEAAAAAAIsAAQACAAAAHwCKAAEA
       QgAAAAUAPAAAAAoAT3BlblN5bWJvbAAAAAAAAPAAAAD//wAAAAAFAAAAAAAAAP8DAAAAAAAA
       AAEA/wMAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIgAAQACAAAAAQCHAAEABQAAAP////8AhgABAAQAAAAAAAAAcgAC
       ABoAAABpAwAA5gAAAAEAAAA9AL8AAAAAAAEAAQA9AIwAAQAAAAAAiwABAAIAAAAfAIoAAQBI
       AAAABQBCAAAAEABMaWJlcmF0aW9uIFNlcmlmAAAAAAAA8AAAAAAAAAAAAAUAAAAAAAIA/wMA
       AAAAAAAAAQD/AwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAiAABAAIAAAABAIcAAQAFAAAA/////wCGAAEABAAAAAAA
       AAByAAIAHQAAADIEAADmAAAAAwBtYXiQAQAAAAADAAMAbQBhAHgAjAABAAAAAACLAAEAAgAA
       AB8AigABAEIAAAAFADwAAAAKAE9wZW5TeW1ib2wAAHcAAAD1AAAA//8AAAAABQAAAAAAAAD/
       AwAAAAAAAAABAP8DAAAAAAB3AAAAAACIAAEAAgAAAAEAhwABAAUAAAD/////AIYAAQAEAAAA
       AAAAAHIAAgAaAAAA6QUAAOEAAAABAAAAKAAoAAAAAAABAAEAKACMAAEAAAAAAIsAAQACAAAA
       HwCKAAEASAAAAAUAQgAAABAATGliZXJhdGlvbiBTZXJpZgAAAAAAAPAAAAAAAAAAAAAFAAAA
       AAAAAP8DAAAAAAAAAAEA/wMAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIgAAQACAAAAAQCHAAEABQAAAP////8AhgAB
       AAQAAAAAAAAAcgACABcAAAAnBgAA5gAAAAEAMHgAAAAAAAEAAQAwAIwAAQAAAAAAiwABAAIA
       AAAfAIoAAQBIAAAABQBCAAAAEABMaWJlcmF0aW9uIFNlcmlmAAAAAAAA8AAAAAAAAAAAAAUA
       AAAAAAIA/wMAAAAAAAAAAQD/AwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAiAABAAIAAAABAIcAAQAFAAAA/////wCG
       AAEABAAAAAAAAAByAAIAFwAAAMAGAADmAAAAAQAsPAAAAAAAAQABACwAjAABAAAAAACLAAEA
       AgAAAB8AigABAEgAAAAFAEIAAAAQAExpYmVyYXRpb24gU2VyaWYAAAAAAADwAAAAAAAAAAAA
       BQAAAAAAAgD/AwAAAAAAAAABAP8DAAAAAAAAAAAAAACIAAEAAgAAAAEAhwABAAUAAAD/////
       AIYAAQAEAAAAAAAAAHIAAgAXAAAAIwcAAOYAAAABAHpdAAAAAAABAAEAegCMAAEAAAAAAIsA
       AQACAAAAHwCKAAEAQgAAAAUAPAAAAAoAT3BlblN5bWJvbAAAdwAAAPUAAAD//wAAAAAFAAAA
       AAAAAP8DAAAAAAAAAAEA/wMAAAAAAHcAAAAAAIgAAQACAAAAAQCHAAEABQAAAP////8AhgAB
       AAQAAAAAAAAAcgACABoAAACcBwAA4QAAAAEAAAApACgAAAAAAAEAAQApAIwAAQAAAAAAjAAB
       AAAAAACMAAEAAAAAAA==
      </office:binary-data>
     </draw:image>
    </draw:frame></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Questa funzione restituisce zero per i valori negativi e lascia invariati quelli positivi. Negli LLM basati su <text:span text:style-name="T41">t</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">ransformer</text:span> è frequente l’uso di funzioni più “morbide”, come GELU, all’interno delle reti <text:span text:style-name="T6">feed-forward</text:span> presenti in ogni strato.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P58" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1590_447025415"/><text:soft-page-break/>Gli strati della rete<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1590_447025415"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">I neuroni sono organizzati in <text:span text:style-name="Strong_20_Emphasis">strati</text:span>. Una rappresentazione semplificata è:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">ingresso</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:s text:c="3"/>↓</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">primo strato</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:s text:c="3"/>↓</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">secondo strato</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:s text:c="3"/>↓</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">...</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:s text:c="3"/>↓</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">uscita</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Ogni strato riceve un vettore di numeri e ne produce un altro. Nei primi strati possono emergere relazioni relativamente semplici; negli strati successivi queste rappresentazioni vengono combinate in strutture più astratte.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Nel caso di un modello linguistico, gli strati possono contribuire a rappresentare caratteristiche lessicali, relazioni grammaticali, dipendenze tra parole, riferimenti tra pronomi e nomi, struttura di una frase, stile e tono, relazioni semantiche, schemi logici o procedurali.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Queste specializzazioni, tuttavia, non sono normalmente rigide né concentrate in un singolo neurone.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P58" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1592_447025415"/>Vettori e matrici<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1592_447025415"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Nelle implementazioni reali, i calcoli non vengono eseguiti neurone per neurone. Gli ingressi, i pesi e le uscite vengono organizzati in vettori e matrici. Uno strato può essere rappresentato schematicamente come:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Object24" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:y="-0.406cm" svg:width="2.357cm" svg:height="0.522cm" draw:z-index="29"><draw:object>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
       <semantics>
        <mrow>
         <mrow>
          <mstyle mathvariant="bold">
           <mi>y</mi>
          </mstyle>
          <mo stretchy="false">=</mo>
          <mi>f</mi>
         </mrow>
         <mrow>
          <mo fence="true" form="prefix" stretchy="true">(</mo>
          <mrow>
           <mrow>
            <mstyle mathvariant="bold">
             <mi>W</mi>
            </mstyle>
            <mrow>
             <mstyle mathvariant="bold">
              <mi>x</mi>
             </mstyle>
             <mo stretchy="false">+</mo>
             <mstyle mathvariant="bold">
              <mi>b</mi>
             </mstyle>
            </mrow>
           </mrow>
          </mrow>
          <mo fence="true" form="postfix" stretchy="true">)</mo>
         </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0">bold y = f left( bold W bold x + bold b right)</annotation>
       </semantics>
      </math>
     </draw:object><draw:image>
      <office:binary-data>VkNMTVRGAQAxAAAAAAAAAAEAGwAAAAkAAAAAAAAAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAATgFAAAo
       AQAARwAAAJYAAQACAAAACQCLAAEAAgAAAP//gQABABAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADcFAAAnAQAAiwAB
       AAIAAAAAGJUAAQAEAAAAAAAAAJYAAQACAAAACQCLAAEAAgAAAB8AigABAEgAAAAFAEIAAAAQ
       AExpYmVyYXRpb24gU2VyaWYAAAAAAADwAAAAAAAAAAAACAAAAAAAAgD/AwAAAAAAAAABAP8D
       AAAAAAAAAAAAAACIAAEAAgAAAAEAhwABAAUAAAD/////AIYAAQAEAAAAAAAAAHIAAgAXAAAA
       JQAAAOYAAAABAHlrAAAAAAABAAEAeQCMAAEAAAAAAIsAAQACAAAAHwCKAAEAQgAAAAUAPAAA
       AAoAT3BlblN5bWJvbAAAAAAAAPAAAAD//wAAAAAFAAAAAAAAAP8DAAAAAAAAAAEA/wMAAAAA
       AAAAAAAAAIgAAQACAAAAAQCHAAEABQAAAP////8AhgABAAQAAAAAAAAAcgACABoAAACkAAAA
       5gAAAAEAAAA9AL8AAAAAAAEAAQA9AIwAAQAAAAAAiwABAAIAAAAfAIoAAQBIAAAABQBCAAAA
       EABMaWJlcmF0aW9uIFNlcmlmAAAAAAAA8AAAAAAAAAAAAAUAAAAAAAIA/wMAAAAAAAAAAQD/
       AwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAiAABAAIAAAABAIcAAQAFAAAA/////wCGAAEABAAAAAAAAAByAAIAFwAA
       AHMBAADmAAAAAQBmQwAAAAAAAQABAGYAjAABAAAAAACLAAEAAgAAAB8AigABAEIAAAAFADwA
       AAAKAE9wZW5TeW1ib2wAAHcAAAD1AAAA//8AAAAABQAAAAAAAAD/AwAAAAAAAAABAP8DAAAA
       AAB3AAAAAACIAAEAAgAAAAEAhwABAAUAAAD/////AIYAAQAEAAAAAAAAAHIAAgAaAAAA+gEA
       AOEAAAABAAAAKAAoAAAAAAABAAEAKACMAAEAAAAAAIsAAQACAAAAHwCKAAEASAAAAAUAQgAA
       ABAATGliZXJhdGlvbiBTZXJpZgAAAAAAAPAAAAAAAAAAAAAIAAAAAAACAP8DAAAAAAAAAAEA
       /wMAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIgAAQACAAAAAQCHAAEABQAAAP////8AhgABAAQAAAAAAAAAcgACABcA
       AAA1AgAA5gAAAAEAV9UAAAAAAAEAAQBXAIwAAQAAAAAAiwABAAIAAAAfAIoAAQBIAAAABQBC
       AAAAEABMaWJlcmF0aW9uIFNlcmlmAAAAAAAA8AAAAAAAAAAAAAgAAAAAAAIA/wMAAAAAAAAA
       AQD/AwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAiAABAAIAAAABAIcAAQAFAAAA/////wCGAAEABAAAAAAAAAByAAIA
       FwAAAE0DAADmAAAAAQB4eAAAAAAAAQABAHgAjAABAAAAAACLAAEAAgAAAB8AigABAEIAAAAF
       ADwAAAAKAE9wZW5TeW1ib2wAAAAAAADwAAAA//8AAAAABQAAAAAAAAD/AwAAAAAAAAABAP8D
       AAAAAAAAAAAAAACIAAEAAgAAAAEAhwABAAUAAAD/////AIYAAQAEAAAAAAAAAHIAAgAaAAAA
       2gMAAOYAAAABAAAAKwCMAAAAAAABAAEAKwCMAAEAAAAAAIsAAQACAAAAHwCKAAEASAAAAAUA
       QgAAABAATGliZXJhdGlvbiBTZXJpZgAAAAAAAPAAAAAAAAAAAAAIAAAAAAACAP8DAAAAAAAA
       AAEA/wMAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIgAAQACAAAAAQCHAAEABQAAAP////8AhgABAAQAAAAAAAAAcgAC
       ABcAAAB9BAAA5gAAAAEAYngAAAAAAAEAAQBiAIwAAQAAAAAAiwABAAIAAAAfAIoAAQBCAAAA
       BQA8AAAACgBPcGVuU3ltYm9sAAB3AAAA9QAAAP//AAAAAAUAAAAAAAAA/wMAAAAAAAAAAQD/
       AwAAAAAAdwAAAAAAiAABAAIAAAABAIcAAQAFAAAA/////wCGAAEABAAAAAAAAAByAAIAGgAA
       AAwFAADhAAAAAQAAACkAKAAAAAAAAQABACkAjAABAAAAAACMAAEAAAAAAIwAAQAAAAAA
      </office:binary-data>
     </draw:image>
    </draw:frame></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">dove:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="L13">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P59"><text:span text:style-name="T4">x</text:span> è il vettore in ingresso;</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P59"><text:span text:style-name="T42">W</text:span> è la matrice dei pesi;</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P59"><text:span text:style-name="T42">b</text:span> è il vettore dei bias;</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P59"><text:span text:style-name="T4">f</text:span> è la funzione di attivazione;</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P59"><text:span text:style-name="T42">y</text:span> è il vettore in uscita.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Gran parte del lavoro computazionale di una rete neurale consiste quindi in moltiplicazioni tra matrici molto grandi. Questo è uno dei motivi per cui GPU e acceleratori specializzati sono particolarmente adatti all’addestramento e all’esecuzione degli LLM.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P58" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1594_447025415"/><text:soft-page-break/>Che cosa sono i parametri?<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1594_447025415"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">I <text:span text:style-name="Strong_20_Emphasis">parametri</text:span> della rete sono principalmente i pesi e i bias. Quando si dice che un modello possiede miliardi di parametri, significa che contiene miliardi di valori numerici regolabili.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Semplificando:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">parametro 1 <text:s text:c="2"/>= <text:s/>0,027</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">parametro 2 <text:s text:c="2"/>= -0,814</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">parametro 3 <text:s text:c="2"/>= <text:s/>1,203</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">...</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Questi numeri non vengono assegnati manualmente da un programmatore. Vengono appresi durante l’addestramento. Un singolo parametro non corrisponde necessariamente a<text:span text:style-name="T43">d</text:span> una conoscenza specifica. Non esiste normalmente un peso isolato che significhi:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P60">Roma è la capitale d’Italia.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Le informazioni sono distribuite tra moltissimi parametri e vengono ricostruite attraverso l’interazione dell’intera rete.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P58" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1596_447025415"/>La propagazione in avanti<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1596_447025415"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Quando il modello riceve un testo, i <text:span text:style-name="T6">token</text:span> vengono trasformati in vettori numerici. Questi vettori attraversano gli strati della rete. Ogni strato modifica la rappresentazione ricevuta e la passa al successivo. Questo processo viene chiamato <text:span text:style-name="Strong_20_Emphasis"><text:span text:style-name="T6">forward pass</text:span></text:span>, o propagazione in avanti:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">token</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:s text:c="2"/>↓</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">embedding</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:s text:c="2"/>↓</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">strato 1</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:s text:c="2"/>↓</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">strato 2</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:s text:c="2"/>↓</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">...</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:s text:c="2"/>↓</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P51"><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text">probabilità del </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"><text:span text:style-name="T6">token</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Source_20_Text"> successivo</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Alla fine, il modello produce un valore per ogni possibile <text:span text:style-name="T6">token</text:span> del proprio vocabolario. Questi valori vengono trasformati in probabilità tramite una funzione come la softmax.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P58" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1598_447025415"/>Come impara la rete<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc1598_447025415"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48">Durante l’addestramento, il modello riceve sequenze di <text:span text:style-name="T6">token</text:span> e cerca di prevedere il <text:span text:style-name="T6">token</text:span> successivo. La previsione viene confrontata con il <text:span text:style-name="T6">token</text:span> corretto e, come visto in precedenza, si calcola una <text:span text:style-name="Strong_20_Emphasis">funzione di perdita</text:span> che misura l’errore.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48"><text:soft-page-break/>A questo punto entra in gioco la <text:span text:style-name="Strong_20_Emphasis"><text:span text:style-name="T6">backpropagation</text:span></text:span> (retropropagazione): partendo dall’errore, si calcola per ogni parametro <draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Object31" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:y="-0.379cm" svg:width="0.316cm" svg:height="0.471cm" draw:z-index="37"><draw:object>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
       <semantics>
        <mi>w</mi>
        <annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0">w</annotation>
       </semantics>
      </math>
     </draw:object><draw:image>
      <office:binary-data>VkNMTVRGAQAxAAAAAAAAAAEAGwAAAAkAAAAAAAAAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAbMAAAAL
       AQAADwAAAJYAAQACAAAACQCLAAEAAgAAAP//gQABABAAAAAAAAAAAAAAALIAAAAKAQAAiwAB
       AAIAAAAAGJUAAQAEAAAAAAAAAJYAAQACAAAACQCLAAEAAgAAAB8AigABAEgAAAAFAEIAAAAQ
       AExpYmVyYXRpb24gU2VyaWYAAAAAAADwAAAAAAAAAAAABQAAAAAAAgD/AwAAAAAAAAABAP8D
       AAAAAAAAAAAAAACIAAEAAgAAAAEAhwABAAUAAAD/////AIYAAQAEAAAAAAAAAHIAAgAXAAAA
       BwAAANcAAAABAHegAAAAAAABAAEAdwCMAAEAAAAAAIwAAQAAAAAAjAABAAAAAAA=
      </office:binary-data>
     </draw:image>
    </draw:frame><text:s/>quanto una sua piccola variazione influenzerebbe la perdita:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Object25" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:y="-0.621cm" svg:width="0.681cm" svg:height="1.004cm" draw:z-index="38"><draw:object>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
       <semantics>
        <mfrac>
         <mrow>
          <mo stretchy="false">∂</mo>
          <mi>L</mi>
         </mrow>
         <mrow>
          <mo stretchy="false">∂</mo>
          <mi>w</mi>
         </mrow>
        </mfrac>
        <annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0">{partial L} over {partial w}</annotation>
       </semantics>
      </math>
     </draw:object><draw:image>
      <office:binary-data>VkNMTVRGAQAxAAAAAAAAAAEAGwAAAAkAAAAAAAAAAAABAAAAAQAAAAEAAAABAAAAAYIBAAA5
