   <text:p text:style-name="P48">L’insieme di queste derivate costituisce il gradiente. I parametri vengono quindi modificati nella direzione che tende a ridurre la perdita. In forma semplificata:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Object30" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:y="-0.621cm" svg:width="3.72cm" svg:height="1.004cm" draw:z-index="39"><draw:object>
      <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
       <semantics>
        <mrow>
         <mrow>
          <msub>
           <mi>w</mi>
           <mi mathvariant="italic">nuovo</mi>
          </msub>
          <mo stretchy="false">=</mo>
          <mrow>
           <msub>
            <mi>w</mi>
            <mi mathvariant="italic">vecchio</mi>
           </msub>
           <mo stretchy="false">−</mo>
           <mi>η</mi>
          </mrow>
         </mrow>
         <mfrac>
          <mrow>
           <mo stretchy="false">∂</mo>
           <mi>L</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow>
           <mo stretchy="false">∂</mo>
           <mi>w</mi>
          </mrow>
         </mfrac>
        </mrow>
        <annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0">w_{nuovo} = w_{vecchio} - %eta {partial L} over {partial w}</annotation>
       </semantics>
      </math>
     </draw:object><draw:image>
